Article 5 (Duties)
(1) Security management personnel shall comply with statutes and faithfully perform their duties in accordance with instructions of the chief officer and on-site managers.
(2) Security management personnel shall not engage in any of the following conduct:
1. Assault, insulting remarks, sexist or sexually harassing remarks, or other conduct that damages the dignity of security management personnel;
2. Leaving the place of duty without permission of the chief officer or an on-site manager;
3. Drinking alcohol, sleeping, or other conduct that interferes with faithful performance of duty;
4. Wearing clothing contrary to applicable regulations;
5. Other conduct violating statutes or matters determined by the Secretary General.
(3) The Secretary General shall have the chief officer and on-site managers supervise the work and service of security management personnel and ensure appropriate measures are taken where any breach of duty occurs.
